00:46:17.380 --> 00:46:55.700
<v Sam Gebler>Yeah, you're out in the middle of the ocean-- not the middle of the ocean. But you're way, way far away from the shore. You can't see the shore anymore. And you're focused on the patient. You're like, all right, how do I get this person to breathe again? And somehow, she just started coughing up all that water. And I just remember the heaving, just the whole-- all the muscles just contracting and just the disgusting heaving and coughing of all this water coming up, up out of her mouth. And you're just like, holy shit. This is real.
<v Sam Gebler>是的，你在海洋中央——不是海洋中央。但你离岸边非常非常远。你已经看不见岸边了。你专注于病人。你心想，好吧，我怎么才能让她重新呼吸？不知何故，她开始咳出所有的水。我只记得那种起伏，整个——所有的肌肉都在收缩，嘴里咳出水的恶心画面。你就像是，圣屎啊。这是真的。

